 their adventure booth reveals  that his father was obsessed with  locating the hidden treasure of hitler's  secret arts and antiquities dealer  unfortunately for some unknown reason  booth's father came to believe that his  son was responsible for the temporary  loss of a prized nazi watch as a result  as he reveals to hartley in prison his  father did not speak to him for more  than a year and their strange  relationship led to booth embracing a  lonely life of crime however throughout  the film booth and hartley become close  after the two escaped the reach of the  police in south america booth is  actually willing to sacrifice the third  egg in order to save his new friend  after hartley and the bishop's betrayal  is revealed though booth quickly sells  them out to interpol freezing their 300  million dollar payout  see  now we're even  if everyone loses no one gets the money  we can all be friends again  booth then takes his new best friends on  a mission to the louvre in paris which  he promises will offer double the payout  and triple the challenge honestly it all  seems like a lot to take on for someone  who just wants to make a few friends  while nolan booth and john hartley both  end up being decidedly different people  than they initially seem to be gal  gadetz the bishop is pretty much exactly  the character she says that she is at  the beginning of red notice she loves to  steal from people and takes joy and  beating booth at every turn while the  film doesn't explore the bishop's  origins nearly as much as it does booths  and hartleys she does share a few  important pieces of information that  make it clear why she turned to a life  of crime in the middle of the film the  bishop holds an intelligence analyst  hostage and treats him as a largely  unwilling therapist during their session  she explains that she also faced a tough  childhood and that her father made her  who she is today she further questions  whether her inability to accept second  place 